WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:09.134
What on earth is that thing...

2
00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:12.637
Let's run!

3
00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:13.555
Wait!

4
00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:14.681
We might get killed.

5
00:00:14.764 --> 00:00:15.807
What do you suggest we do then?

6
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.183
Is there no other way out?

7
00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.601
How would I know?

8
00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.894
Two people are already dead.

9
00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:21.229
Everyone. don't move.

10
00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:23.398
If we move rashly.
the statue will attack again!

11
00:00:28.319 --> 00:00:30.447
Joohee.

12
00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:32.282
That was close.

13
00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:35.493
If you didn't notice
the statue's movement.

14
00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.037
we'd all be dead by now.

15
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.204
What?

16
00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:40.623
You told us to get down
because you knew it. right?

17
00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.666
No.

18
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.668
I just sensed an imminent threat...

19
00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.296
Mr. Song!

20
00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.255
Your hand...

21
00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:50.175
I can still bear it.

22
00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:51.843
Can you help me stop the bleeding?

23
00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.640
I should have asked Joohee to treat me.

24
00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.517
But she's too weak-minded.

25
00:01:00.268 --> 00:01:01.686
That's why she can only participate in
simple missions

26
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.522
despite being a B-Rank healer.

27
00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:08.985
I've also participated in
a couple of B-rank missions.

28
00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:11.821
But that thing might be an A-rank one.

29
00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.449
or even an S-rank one.

30
00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:18.912
The commandments of the Cartenon Temple
written on the stone.

31
00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:21.456
First. worship the God.

32
00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:23.666
Second. praise the God.

33
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.044
Third. believe the God.

34
00:01:26.127 --> 00:01:27.670
Those who do not abide
by these commandments

35
00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.464
will not leave this place alive.

36
00:01:29.547 --> 00:01:30.590
Mr. Song.

37
00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:32.091
The god mentioned

38
00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.219
should be it. right?

39
00:01:36.179 --> 00:01:38.181
More than a decade ago.

40
00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:43.394
portals that could connect to a different
dimension suddenly appeared in the world.

41
00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:47.065
Abnormal phenomena kept
occurring around the world.

42
00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:54.030
For example. The Awakened
are known as hunters.

43
00:01:54.656 --> 00:02:00.203
Hunters are responsible for killing magic
beasts in dungeons within the portals.

44
00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:04.541
And after hunters awaken.
their abilities will not change.

45
00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:09.462
However. sometimes on
the other side of the portal.

46
00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:15.844
there are terrifying monsters
that bring despair.

47
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

48
00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.229
Did you see that?

49
00:03:49.312 --> 00:03:50.396
That film?

50
00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.066
What are you doing?

51
00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:54.901
Class is about to start.

52
00:03:54.984 --> 00:03:55.902
Something came up.

53
00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:01.532
Jinah. your brother is a hunter. right?

54
00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:02.575
Right.

55
00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:05.203
But he's just an E-rank hunter.

56
00:04:05.286 --> 00:04:07.956
He always ends up being covered in wounds.

57
00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:10.333
Last time he was covered in bandages.

58
00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.670
But why do you ask me this?

59
00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:14.754
No reason.

60
00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.216
If it were me. I wouldn't
have ended up like that.

61
00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.678
We can't possibly be its opponent.

62
00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.138
Let's get out once
the situation settles down.

63
00:04:24.222 --> 00:04:26.724
- Although it might not be that easy...
- I can't just sit here and die!

64
00:04:26.808 --> 00:04:30.186
I finally managed to sign a contract
with a large association.

65
00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.939
I can't die in this kind of place.

66
00:04:33.022 --> 00:04:35.024
What are you doing? Don't move!

67
00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:35.942
I can do it.

68
00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:38.027
I'm very confident in my speed.

69
00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.946
I can rush out before it attacks.

70
00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.333
Damn it!

71
00:04:54.168 --> 00:04:57.755
It can finish us off at any time.

72
00:04:57.839 --> 00:05:02.051
As easy as crushing an ant.

73
00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.555
So why isn't it doing it now?

74
00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:09.225
It has the ability to kill us.
but it isn't making a move.

75
00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:13.313
It's different from those magic beasts
that attack blindly.

76
00:05:15.898 --> 00:05:17.025
Mr. Song.

77
00:05:17.108 --> 00:05:18.901
What is the first commandment?

78
00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.028
Commandment?

79
00:05:20.111 --> 00:05:21.529
The first one is...

80
00:05:22.196 --> 00:05:23.364
Worship the God.

81
00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:25.825
God.

82
00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.120
This dungeon has its own rules.

83
00:05:29.203 --> 00:05:31.205
What... what are you doing?

84
00:05:31.289 --> 00:05:32.665
If I'm not wrong...

85
00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:34.917
Hey. stop it...

86
00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:41.716
You don't look like you're seeking death.

87
00:05:58.399 --> 00:05:59.442
Everyone.

88
00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.152
Kneel to the statue!

89
00:06:01.235 --> 00:06:03.154
Huh? Kneel to it?

90
00:06:03.237 --> 00:06:04.614
What nonsense are you talking about?

91
00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.741
Did you figure out something?

92
00:06:06.824 --> 00:06:07.950
Yes.

93
00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:11.746
As long as our heads are below
a certain height. it won't attack.

94
00:06:11.829 --> 00:06:14.415
This is probably the meaning
of the first commandment.

95
00:06:18.961 --> 00:06:21.005
Are you sure?

96
00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:22.757
Yes. sort of...

97
00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:25.218
If so...

98
00:06:31.015 --> 00:06:32.892
Will we really survive

99
00:06:32.975 --> 00:06:34.143
by just doing this?

100
00:06:41.609 --> 00:06:43.027
Its expression is terrifying.

101
00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:45.571
Its expression changed.

102
00:06:48.282 --> 00:06:49.826
It's not attacking us.

103
00:06:50.993 --> 00:06:52.703
Hey. if you move around...

104
00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.250
Look.

105
00:06:57.333 --> 00:06:59.001
it has stopped attacking.

106
00:07:00.962 --> 00:07:02.755
Is it over just like that?

107
00:07:02.839 --> 00:07:04.048
Are we saved?

108
00:07:04.132 --> 00:07:04.966
We made it.

109
00:07:05.049 --> 00:07:06.175
We're saved.

110
00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:08.052
I can go back alive.

111
00:07:08.136 --> 00:07:08.970
No...

112
00:07:09.554 --> 00:07:10.555
It's not over yet.

113
00:07:17.645 --> 00:07:19.772
It's not over?

114
00:07:19.856 --> 00:07:21.566
Sung. what's next?

115
00:07:21.649 --> 00:07:23.276
Can you think of something?

116
00:07:23.359 --> 00:07:25.820
I... I don't know.

117
00:07:27.905 --> 00:07:30.783
I think we can't violate
the commandments here.

118
00:07:30.867 --> 00:07:32.493
The second commandment
is "Praise the God".

119
00:07:32.577 --> 00:07:33.578
This is the clue.

120
00:07:33.661 --> 00:07:34.704
Praise?

121
00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:36.330
How?

122
00:07:36.414 --> 00:07:38.124
Leave it to me.

123
00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:41.586
I am conducting research
on traditional folklore.

124
00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:44.547
I know how to praise God.

125
00:07:47.383 --> 00:07:48.885
Lord.

126
00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:50.970
The ruler who brings order to the world.

127
00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:52.972
Any reaction?

128
00:07:53.055 --> 00:07:55.057
- Bestow your light upon my feeble heart.
- It seems to have slowed down...

129
00:07:55.766 --> 00:07:58.269
Guide me to the path of truth.

130
00:07:58.352 --> 00:07:59.312
Wait!

131
00:07:59.395 --> 00:08:00.563
This is...

132
00:08:01.189 --> 00:08:03.941
I wish to follow the will of God.

133
00:08:05.026 --> 00:08:07.278
These are not the words
to praise this god.

134
00:08:07.904 --> 00:08:10.448
We will worship and honor you.

135
00:08:10.531 --> 00:08:12.074
Lord.

136
00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.577
The ruler who brings order to the world.

137
00:08:19.874 --> 00:08:20.791
Damn it!

138
00:08:20.875 --> 00:08:22.168
Run!

139
00:08:30.218 --> 00:08:31.385
It's dangerous to be together.

140
00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:32.386
Scatter!

141
00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:33.387
Alright.

142
00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:35.848
Joohee. run!

143
00:08:37.892 --> 00:08:40.353
How can I die in a place like this?

144
00:08:40.436 --> 00:08:42.522
My family is still waiting for me!

145
00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:46.108
I should be safe here. right?

146
00:08:46.609 --> 00:08:48.653
Hey. Park. behind you!

147
00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.331
Park!

148
00:09:01.374 --> 00:09:04.043
Praise the God...

149
00:09:04.835 --> 00:09:07.672
What should we praise about it?

150
00:09:07.755 --> 00:09:09.549
It's essentially a demon.

151
00:09:10.424 --> 00:09:11.300
But...

152
00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.928
I can't just abandon her.

153
00:09:16.472 --> 00:09:17.723
Is there any clue...

154
00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:19.392
Gun.

155
00:09:20.017 --> 00:09:20.935
Axe.

156
00:09:21.018 --> 00:09:23.646
My hand... my hand!

157
00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:25.481
Hammer.

158
00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:26.732
Sword.

159
00:09:26.816 --> 00:09:27.650
Musical instrument.

160
00:09:28.484 --> 00:09:29.527
Musical instrument...

161
00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:36.075
Everyone. get under the statue
holding a musical instrument!

162
00:09:36.158 --> 00:09:37.410
Musical instrument.

163
00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.126
Is it playing?

164
00:09:45.209 --> 00:09:49.005
The statue holding a musical
instrument won't attack us!

165
00:09:57.138 --> 00:09:58.472
Damn it.

166
00:10:00.141 --> 00:10:01.350
Start playing quickly!

167
00:10:01.434 --> 00:10:02.685
Come on!

168
00:10:03.644 --> 00:10:05.980
Two people can't stand here together?

169
00:10:06.063 --> 00:10:07.815
Joohee. stay here!

170
00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:09.442
Jinwoo!

171
00:10:19.076 --> 00:10:20.161
Over there.

172
00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.880
Not there!

173
00:10:34.258 --> 00:10:35.760
No!

174
00:10:35.843 --> 00:10:37.887
Jinwoo!

175
00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:51.609
It's not over yet.

176
00:10:55.071 --> 00:10:55.946
It's not...

177
00:11:17.301 --> 00:11:19.929
Is this the answer to praise the God?

178
00:11:26.185 --> 00:11:27.061
Jinwoo!

179
00:11:27.645 --> 00:11:28.687
Are you okay?

180
00:11:29.647 --> 00:11:31.273
Yes. I'm fine.

181
00:11:36.987 --> 00:11:38.489
Jinwoo.

182
00:11:38.572 --> 00:11:39.907
What is the matter?

183
00:11:44.245 --> 00:11:45.287
Your foot...

184
00:11:48.416 --> 00:11:50.793
It's enough. Joohee.

185
00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:52.878
I'm okay now.

186
00:11:52.962 --> 00:11:54.505
What are you talking about?

187
00:11:54.588 --> 00:11:56.215
I'll definitely cure you.

188
00:11:59.969 --> 00:12:01.220
Joohee.

189
00:12:03.013 --> 00:12:04.432
So tragic...

190
00:12:04.932 --> 00:12:06.058
Indeed.

191
00:12:07.685 --> 00:12:09.311
I'm very sorry that you lost your arm.

192
00:12:09.895 --> 00:12:12.815
As the captain. you made a hasty decision.

193
00:12:12.898 --> 00:12:14.233
This is karma.

194
00:12:14.316 --> 00:12:15.151
How cruel.

195
00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:16.068
It's because Mr. Kim...

196
00:12:16.152 --> 00:12:17.570
Wasn't it a unanimous decision to come in?

197
00:12:18.154 --> 00:12:19.780
You voted in favor. didn't you?

198
00:12:20.781 --> 00:12:24.034
Indeed. it was me who
made the final decision.

199
00:12:24.702 --> 00:12:26.620
I must bear all the responsibility.

200
00:12:27.329 --> 00:12:29.707
Now is not the time to argue.

201
00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:31.333
There is still one commandment
that has not been solved.

202
00:12:33.752 --> 00:12:35.087
What's happening this time?

203
00:12:35.171 --> 00:12:36.380
An earthquake?

204
00:12:39.216 --> 00:12:40.509
What... What is that?

205
00:12:41.135 --> 00:12:42.219
An altar...

206
00:12:43.721 --> 00:12:46.599
Doesn't it often appear in mythology?

207
00:12:46.682 --> 00:12:49.435
It's for offering tributes
or living sacrifices to the god.

208
00:12:49.518 --> 00:12:52.396
The third commandment
is "Believe the God".

209
00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:57.610
I might be ignorant. but I know
what this means.

210
00:12:58.360 --> 00:12:59.862
Sung.

211
00:12:59.945 --> 00:13:03.157
We need to offer a sacrifice. right?

212
00:13:05.159 --> 00:13:10.080
My companion. who bragged about his wife
before departure. was cut in half.

213
00:13:10.164 --> 00:13:11.749
There were others too.

214
00:13:12.458 --> 00:13:14.668
Do you remember what you just said?

215
00:13:14.752 --> 00:13:16.045
Now it's your turn to take responsibility.

216
00:13:16.128 --> 00:13:16.962
Captain.

217
00:13:17.046 --> 00:13:18.297
How can you. Mr. Kim...

218
00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:19.548
Sung. shut up.

219
00:13:21.091 --> 00:13:22.176
I understand...

220
00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:24.887
Let me go alone.

221
00:13:26.889 --> 00:13:29.141
It's not just his fault.

222
00:13:29.225 --> 00:13:31.393
We all voted to come in here.

223
00:13:35.397 --> 00:13:37.191
What's the situation now?

224
00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.154
Sung.

225
00:13:42.238 --> 00:13:44.615
Is there something else I need to do?

226
00:13:44.698 --> 00:13:46.408
What does this mean?

227
00:13:46.492 --> 00:13:48.702
Doesn't it want a living sacrifice?

228
00:13:50.037 --> 00:13:51.580
I'm sorry.

229
00:13:51.664 --> 00:13:55.501
I'd like to check the altar.
Can you help me over there?

230
00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.630
Please take me near the altar.

231
00:13:59.713 --> 00:14:01.632
But in this case...

232
00:14:01.715 --> 00:14:03.551
I don't think anything will happen.

233
00:14:10.516 --> 00:14:12.601
Have you figured out anything?

234
00:14:12.685 --> 00:14:13.894
No. not yet...

235
00:14:14.687 --> 00:14:18.232
If we wait here. will someone
come to rescue us?

236
00:14:18.315 --> 00:14:20.734
Today is the seventh day
after the dungeon was created.

237
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.113
I think they will take action
before we are rescued.

238
00:14:27.533 --> 00:14:30.494
The portal will be fully open
after seven days.

239
00:14:32.663 --> 00:14:34.456
And that is "Dungeon Break".

240
00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:38.919
Then. the magic beasts will pass through
the portal to the human world.

241
00:14:39.837 --> 00:14:44.550
That's why we must defeat the Boss and
close the portal within the time limit.

242
00:14:44.633 --> 00:14:46.510
This is another purpose
of the raid mission.

243
00:14:47.344 --> 00:14:50.347
If we fail here.

244
00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.976
the beasts will run out into the world.

245
00:14:54.935 --> 00:14:56.186
Hello.

246
00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:57.563
Miss Sung.

247
00:14:57.646 --> 00:14:59.106
You come every day.

248
00:15:05.613 --> 00:15:08.198
Mother. it's me again.

249
00:15:08.282 --> 00:15:10.910
Let me tell you. Song-Yi was late today.

250
00:15:10.993 --> 00:15:12.870
She said something kept her.

251
00:15:12.953 --> 00:15:14.914
but she definitely overslept.

252
00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:19.293
And the last nationwide exam...

253
00:15:23.464 --> 00:15:25.215
Please come over here. you two.

254
00:15:25.925 --> 00:15:29.136
This way. we should be able to light
the corresponding number of flames.

255
00:15:29.219 --> 00:15:32.014
Only then will we know what will happen.

256
00:15:47.655 --> 00:15:48.948
The door is open.

257
00:15:49.448 --> 00:15:50.658
Can we go out now?

258
00:15:50.741 --> 00:15:52.159
Can this be a trap...

259
00:15:57.539 --> 00:15:58.582
What is this sound?

260
00:15:58.666 --> 00:16:00.918
The... the statues are coming this way.

261
00:16:01.001 --> 00:16:02.419
What should we do?

262
00:16:03.003 --> 00:16:04.713
Why are they walking towards us?

263
00:16:10.052 --> 00:16:11.095
No!

264
00:16:11.178 --> 00:16:13.097
Joohee. don't close your eyes.

265
00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:14.723
Once we look away. they'll move closer.

266
00:16:15.724 --> 00:16:18.060
It's like the game
we used to play as kids.

267
00:16:18.143 --> 00:16:20.354
Everyone must keep their eyes
fixed on the statues.

268
00:16:33.575 --> 00:16:34.493
No!

269
00:16:34.576 --> 00:16:35.869
- Hey!
- Wait!

270
00:16:40.708 --> 00:16:42.084
Sung. what is this?

271
00:16:42.167 --> 00:16:45.546
The door closed a bit.
but she made it out.

272
00:16:45.629 --> 00:16:47.047
What's going on...

273
00:16:47.131 --> 00:16:49.925
The blue flames will go out over time.

274
00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:53.137
And once someone leaves the altar.
the orange flames will also go out.

275
00:16:53.887 --> 00:16:55.806
The first commandment is "worship".

276
00:16:56.598 --> 00:16:58.017
The second is "praise".

277
00:16:58.809 --> 00:17:00.269
The third is "believe".

278
00:17:01.812 --> 00:17:03.564
That door must be a trap.

279
00:17:03.647 --> 00:17:06.734
It offers false optimism
to us who are in terror.

280
00:17:06.817 --> 00:17:10.112
Perhaps it tests our faith
in God in this way.

281
00:17:10.195 --> 00:17:11.780
So... sorry.

282
00:17:11.864 --> 00:17:13.323
I can't hold on any longer.

283
00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:16.869
- Jungho!
- Hey!

284
00:17:18.954 --> 00:17:19.830
No!

285
00:17:25.085 --> 00:17:26.295
Everyone. don't move!

286
00:17:26.378 --> 00:17:28.756
If anyone else leaves.
it will create a blind spot!

287
00:17:29.631 --> 00:17:31.300
Sung. what does this mean?

288
00:17:31.383 --> 00:17:32.509
Explain it!

289
00:17:32.593 --> 00:17:36.847
Just keep it this way. and don't move
your gaze away from the statue.

290
00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.682
The blue flame is a timer.

291
00:17:38.766 --> 00:17:41.226
When it goes out completely.
everyone should be able to escape.

292
00:17:42.436 --> 00:17:43.604
But. Sung...

293
00:17:44.188 --> 00:17:48.358
It's also possible that when the flame
goes out completely. we'll be locked up.

294
00:17:49.943 --> 00:17:51.236
To be honest.

295
00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:54.990
I never thought that you
would be so active as the weakest one.

296
00:17:55.074 --> 00:17:57.743
We can survive until now

297
00:17:57.826 --> 00:17:59.119
all thanks to you.

298
00:17:59.828 --> 00:18:00.746
Mr. Kim...

299
00:18:02.289 --> 00:18:03.332
But you see.

300
00:18:03.415 --> 00:18:05.417
I have family waiting for me.

301
00:18:05.501 --> 00:18:07.753
I don't want to die yet.

302
00:18:07.836 --> 00:18:10.172
I want to go home alive.

303
00:18:10.255 --> 00:18:12.841
I can't hold on any longer.

304
00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:14.384
I'm sorry.

305
00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:20.891
Why...

306
00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:23.936
I won't give up.

307
00:18:24.019 --> 00:18:25.437
I must survive.

308
00:18:26.688 --> 00:18:29.483
I have always survived this way.

309
00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:35.239
You two. leave quickly.

310
00:18:36.198 --> 00:18:37.407
Mr. Song...

311
00:18:37.491 --> 00:18:42.621
I think as long as one person stays.
that door won't close.

312
00:18:42.704 --> 00:18:45.666
Then. I should let the young people
with promising futures leave first.

313
00:18:45.749 --> 00:18:47.793
Joohee. please take care of Sung.

314
00:18:47.876 --> 00:18:49.253
Okay!

315
00:18:51.463 --> 00:18:54.216
Strange...

316
00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:55.801
My leg...

317
00:18:55.884 --> 00:18:57.511
I can't move it.

318
00:18:58.804 --> 00:19:01.265
You've overexerted yourself
when treating Sung.

319
00:19:02.141 --> 00:19:03.267
Mr. Song.

320
00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.144
Take Joohee and leave.

321
00:19:05.227 --> 00:19:06.979
What? I said I would stay...

322
00:19:07.062 --> 00:19:09.606
Then who will help Joohee out?

323
00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:11.441
There's no time. hurry up!

324
00:19:11.942 --> 00:19:14.027
No... No... Jinwoo...

325
00:19:14.111 --> 00:19:15.070
Let me stay!

326
00:19:15.154 --> 00:19:17.865
I promised I would take
you out to eat. right?

327
00:19:18.907 --> 00:19:20.409
Use this to buy something to eat.

328
00:19:20.909 --> 00:19:22.161
After I get out.

329
00:19:22.244 --> 00:19:23.912
I'll come to you for
the rest of the money.

330
00:19:23.996 --> 00:19:25.664
How can you still joke...

331
00:19:27.875 --> 00:19:29.042
I'm sorry.

332
00:19:29.126 --> 00:19:31.670
We're really running out of time.

333
00:19:31.753 --> 00:19:33.255
I'll leave her in your care.

334
00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:34.715
Alright.

335
00:19:40.637 --> 00:19:41.597
Great.

336
00:19:42.097 --> 00:19:43.640
Luckily. I am the only one
who's going to die.

337
00:19:45.475 --> 00:19:47.019
If I had known.

338
00:19:47.102 --> 00:19:49.730
I would have bought more insurance.

339
00:19:55.652 --> 00:19:58.322
At least one of you will have
to accompany me on the way.

340
00:19:59.448 --> 00:20:00.741
Come at me!

341
00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:14.755
I'm always the weakest.

342
00:20:15.464 --> 00:20:17.633
People around me always
keep ridiculing me.

343
00:20:18.175 --> 00:20:20.260
But I've tried my best to make it through.

344
00:20:24.765 --> 00:20:25.766
But...

345
00:20:27.351 --> 00:20:28.227
Are you kidding me...

346
00:20:29.102 --> 00:20:31.271
Are you kidding me...

347
00:20:33.315 --> 00:20:35.859
I want to become stronger too.

348
00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:38.820
But I can't.

349
00:20:43.617 --> 00:20:45.577
Despite that.

350
00:20:45.661 --> 00:20:48.247
I've survived up to now in my own way.

351
00:20:53.418 --> 00:20:54.378
Are you...

352
00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:56.672
You can't hold on anymore?

353
00:20:56.755 --> 00:20:59.174
We are all suffering.

354
00:20:59.258 --> 00:21:01.718
You're just justifying yourself.

355
00:21:04.805 --> 00:21:07.224
All the gratitude is just lip service.

356
00:21:07.307 --> 00:21:11.603
It's always the selfish ones
who get all the benefits.

357
00:21:12.187 --> 00:21:13.730
I have a family too.

358
00:21:13.814 --> 00:21:16.692
I want to return home alive too.

359
00:21:23.657 --> 00:21:26.034
"Luckily. I'm the only one
who's going to die?"

360
00:21:32.916 --> 00:21:36.003
Stop it. hypocrite.

361
00:21:39.298 --> 00:21:40.674
Don't...

362
00:21:41.341 --> 00:21:42.801
I don't want to die.

363
00:21:49.266 --> 00:21:50.142
If...

364
00:21:51.393 --> 00:21:53.687
If I could have another chance...

364
00:21:54.305 --> 00:22:54.604
